   "id": "MXIZBDsCZdIY",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "MXIZBDsCZdIY"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Question 2: Group Anagrams\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `group_anagrams(words)` that takes a list of words and returns a list of groups, where each group contains the words that are anagrams of each other.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `group_anagrams([\"eat\", \"tea\", \"tan\", \"ate\", \"nat\", \"bat\"])` returns `[[\"eat\", \"tea\", \"ate\"], [\"tan\", \"nat\"], [\"bat\"]]`. The order of the groups and of the words inside a group does not matter.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "NIR-USDpZdIY",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "NIR-USDpZdIY"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[['eat', 'tea', 'ate'], ['tan', 'nat'], ['bat']]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from collections import defaultdict\n",
    "\n",
    "def group_anagrams(words):\n",
    "    groups = defaultdict(list)\n",
    "    for w in words:\n",
    "        groups[\"\".join(sorted(w))].append(w)\n",
    "    return list(groups.values())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(group_anagrams([\"eat\", \"tea\", \"tan\", \"ate\", \"nat\", \"bat\"]))"
   ]
  },
