    "## Question 3: Two Sum\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `two_sum(nums, target)` that returns a tuple of the indices of two different elements of `nums` that add up to `target`. If no such pair exists, return `None`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `two_sum([2, 7, 11, 15], 9)` returns `(0, 1)`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "6ku63CwyZdIZ",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "6ku63CwyZdIZ"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(0, 1) None\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def two_sum(nums, target):\n",
    "    seen = {}\n",
    "    for i, n in enumerate(nums):\n",
    "        if target - n in seen:\n",
    "            return (seen[target - n], i)\n",
    "        seen[n] = i\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "print(two_sum([2, 7, 11, 15], 9), two_sum([1, 2], 10))"
   ]
  },
  {
