   "id": "J2V_SRQEZdIZ",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "J2V_SRQEZdIZ"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Question 4: Run-Length Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `compress(s)` that compresses a string by replacing each run of the same character with the character followed by the length of the run.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `compress(\"aaabccdddd\")` returns `\"a3b1c2d4\"`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "jjbS7b9FZdIZ",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "jjbS7b9FZdIZ"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "a3b1c2d4 ''\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from itertools import groupby\n",
    "\n",
    "def compress(s):\n",
    "    return \"\".join(f\"{ch}{len(list(g))}\" for ch, g in groupby(s))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(compress(\"aaabccdddd\"), repr(compress(\"\")))"
   ]
  },
