    "## Question 6: Merge Intervals\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `merge_intervals(intervals)` that takes a list of `[start, end]` intervals in any order and returns a list of intervals where all overlapping intervals have been merged, sorted by start.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `merge_intervals([[8, 10], [1, 3], [2, 6], [15, 18]])` returns `[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "FB9oRxbXZdIa",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "FB9oRxbXZdIa"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def merge_intervals(intervals):\n",
    "    merged = []\n",
    "    for s, e in sorted(intervals):\n",
    "        if merged and s <= merged[-1][1]:\n",
    "            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], e)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            merged.append([s, e])\n",
    "    return merged\n",
    "\n",
    "print(merge_intervals([[8, 10], [1, 3], [2, 6], [15, 18]]))"
   ]
  },
