    "## Question 7: Flatten a Nested List\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `flatten(lst)` that takes a list that may contain other lists nested to any depth and returns a single flat list with all the values in their original order.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `flatten([1, [2, [3, [4]], 5]])` returns `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "r8wwmprCZdIa",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "r8wwmprCZdIa"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def flatten(lst):\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for x in lst:\n",
    "        if isinstance(x, list):\n",
    "            out.extend(flatten(x))\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            out.append(x)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "print(flatten([1, [2, [3, [4]], 5]]))"
   ]
  },
