    "## Question 8: Rotate a Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `rotate_matrix(matrix)` that takes a square matrix (a list of lists) and returns a new matrix rotated 90 degrees clockwise.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `rotate_matrix([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]])` returns `[[7, 4, 1], [8, 5, 2], [9, 6, 3]]`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "l2rLKP1aZdIb",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "l2rLKP1aZdIb"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[7, 4, 1], [8, 5, 2], [9, 6, 3]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def rotate_matrix(matrix):\n",
    "    return [list(row) for row in zip(*matrix[::-1])]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(rotate_matrix([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]))"
   ]
