    "## Question 9: Top K Words\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `top_k_words(text, k)` that returns the `k` most frequent words in `text` as a list of `(word, count)` tuples, from most to least frequent. Ignore case and punctuation. If two words have the same count, put the one that comes first alphabetically first.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: `top_k_words(\"The cat and the hat. The cat sat!\", 2)` returns `[(\"the\", 3), (\"cat\", 2)]`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "0Bzv7VF5ZdIb",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "0Bzv7VF5ZdIb"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[('the', 3), ('cat', 2)]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "\n",
    "def top_k_words(text, k):\n",
    "    counts = Counter(re.findall(r\"[a-z0-9']+\", text.lower()))\n",
    "    return sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))[:k]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(top_k_words(\"The cat and the hat. The cat sat!\", 2))"
   ]
  },
  {
